  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Illinois has received $9.1B in federal contract obligations so far in FY2026 to date. The state recorded 396,435 awards with an average award size of $22.9K. Obligations fell 26.6% year over year. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer in Illinois, obligating $4.6B, followed by the Department of Energy with $1.8B and the Department of Veterans Affairs with $1.6B. UCHICAGO ARGONNE, LLC is the largest vendor by obligations at $1B, followed by W S DARLEY & CO at $982M and MEDLINE INDUSTRIES, LP at $773M. Medical, Dental, and Hospital Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences are the top industries, each with $1B in obligations. FY2026 obligations to date sit below the FY25 total of $12.4B and the FY24 total of $13.4B, reflecting the year-over-year decline. These figures are fiscal year to date and represent contract obligations only.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2026 contract spending in Illinois compare to prior fiscal years?",
        "body": "FY2026 to date obligations are $9.1B, below FY25 obligations of $12.4B and below FY24 obligations of $13.4B. Obligations peaked at $13.6B in FY22 and have trended down to the current FY2026 to date total. The year-over-year change is down 26.6%."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and industries dominate federal contracting in Illinois?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense leads buying in Illinois with $4.6B in obligations, followed by the Department of Energy with $1.8B and the Department of Veterans Affairs with $1.6B. Medical equipment wholesalers and research and development in the physical, engineering, and life sciences are the largest industries, each with $1B in obligations. Those industries align with top vendors such as UCHICAGO ARGONNE, LLC at $1B and MEDLINE INDUSTRIES, LP at $773M."
      }
    ]
